-- Every remaining US state gets a form template row.
--
-- Generated by scripts/generate-state-templates.py from researched state
-- documentation rules, on 2026-09-07. Regenerate rather than
-- hand-editing: the generator is where the tiering rule lives.
--
-- ===========================================================================
-- READ THIS BEFORE SELLING ANYTHING ON THE BACK OF IT
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- These rows are NOT fifty state-issued forms. Almost no state publishes one;
-- Virginia's DBHDS Form #680 is the exception, not the pattern. What a state
-- publishes, if anything, is a rule saying what service documentation must
-- contain, and the layout is left to the provider.
--
-- So the rows below come in two tiers, and the tier is visible on the page.
--
-- TIER 1 — 27 state(s) whose citation was independently verified.
--   scripts/verify-citations.py fetched the state's own code site, confirmed
--   the rule number appears there, and confirmed a verbatim quotation from
--   the rule appears there too. The footer cites the rule and says plainly
--   that it is not a state-issued form.
