--
-- TIER 2 — 22 state(s) shipping with no citation at all.
--   Either no rule was found, or what was found could not be verified against
--   the state's own site. These print exactly what the GENERIC template
--   prints: a complete, defensible progress note that names no state and
--   cites no rule. That is the honest output for a rule nobody has read, and
--   it is materially better than the alternative -- an agency in one state
--   filing a document that carries another state's form number.
--
--   An agency in a tier 2 state can still sign up and work. Nothing about
--   their document is wrong; it simply makes no regulatory claim.
--
-- WHAT SALES MAY SAY
--   Tier 1: "we file to your state's rule, and here is the rule."
--   Tier 2: "we'll build your state in if you're first."
--   Neither tier may ever be described as "we have your state's form".
--
-- Rules change. Every citation here was checked on the generation date above
-- and has not been re-checked since. Whoever sells into a tier 1 state should
-- re-read the rule first.
--
-- `schema` is selected from the GENERIC row rather than copied, so all of
-- these share one body of prompts and grounding vocabulary.

